index 0000000..61974b9
--- /dev/null
+++ b/paypal-plan.md
@@ -0,0 +1,64 @@
+# PayPal checkout contract (hardened)
+
+## Amounts
+- Catalog prices are integer cents. The only cents→PayPal conversion is
+  `centsToPayPalAmount` in `lib/paypal.js` (4900 → `"49.00"`, 5 → `"0.05"`).
+- Currency is always server-fixed `USD`. Browser-sent `price`, `amount`,
+  `total`, `currency`, or per-item prices are ignored everywhere.
+
+## `POST /api/paypal/orders`
+- Request: `{ items: [{ sku, qty }] }` only (qty integer 1–10, known SKUs).
+- Server prices the bag, creates the shop order first (`pending`), then
+  creates the PayPal order with `purchase_units[0].custom_id = <shop order id>`,
+  an `items[]` breakdown whose `unit_amount × quantity` sums to
+  `amount.breakdown.item_total.value === amount.value`.
+- The PayPal order id is stored as the shop order's `payment_reference`
+  (unique, partial index in `lib/db.js`).
+- Response: `{ id: <PayPal order id>, orderId: <shop order id> }`.
+- On PayPal failure: shop order is marked `failed`, response is an error
+  object `{ error, issue, debug_id?, orderId }` (4xx from PayPal preserved,
+  otherwise 502). Nothing is paid or shipped.
+
+## `POST /api/paypal/orders/:id/capture`
+Changed from the naive version: previously it returned
+`{ orderId, status: <raw PayPal order status> }` and marked the order paid
+unconditionally. Now:
+- Success: `{ orderId, status: "fulfilled" }` — only after PayPal returns a
+  capture with status `COMPLETED` whose amount (parsed back to cents) and
+  currency equal the shop order total/currency and whose `custom_id`, when
+  echoed by PayPal, equals the shop order id. Fulfilment is claimed
+  atomically (`pending → paid` only for one caller), so it ships once.
+- Capture `PENDING`: `202 { orderId, status: "pending", error }`; the order
+  stays `pending` until a verified `PAYMENT.CAPTURE.COMPLETED` webhook.
+- `INSTRUMENT_DECLINED` (422): `{ error: "…choose another way to pay.", issue, debug_id?, orderId, restart: true }`; order stays `pending`.
+- `TRANSACTION_REFUSED` and other PayPal errors: same `{ error, issue, debug_id?, orderId }`
+  shape with PayPal's status (or 502); order stays unpaid, never fulfilled.
+- `ORDER_ALREADY_CAPTURED` or an unknown/5xx outcome: the server re-reads
+  the order from PayPal (`GET /v2/checkout/orders/:id`) and settles only
+  from what PayPal holds. Re-capturing a paid/fulfilled order answers
+  `{ orderId, status }` without shipping again.
+- Unknown PayPal order id for this shop: `404 { error: "unknown order" }`.
+- Outside live (`PAYPAL_ENV != "live"`), a caller's `PayPal-Mock-Response`
+  header is forwarded to PayPal for sandbox negative testing.
+
+## `POST /api/paypal/webhooks`
+- Every delivery is verified first via
+  `POST /v1/notifications/verify-webhook-signature` (client-credentials
+  token, header fields + `PAYPAL_WEBHOOK_ID` + parsed body). Anything other
+  than `verification_status: "SUCCESS"` → `400`, no state change.
+- Event ids are recorded once (`webhook_events.event_id` primary key);
+  repeat deliveries → `200`, no change.
+- Only verified `PAYMENT.CAPTURE.COMPLETED` with matching amount/currency
+  (and `custom_id` when present) settles an order, via the same atomic
+  claim. `CHECKOUT.ORDER.APPROVED` is acknowledged (`200`) and never marks
+  anything paid; paid/fulfilled orders never move backwards.
+
+## Browser (Web SDK v6)
+- `GET /api/paypal/config` returns only `{ clientId, environment, sdkScriptUrl, testBuyerCountry, currency }` — never the secret. The SDK script URL is chosen from `PAYPAL_ENV`, not from the API base URL.
+- PayPal, Venmo and Pay Later buttons are web components shown only when
+  `findEligibleMethods` says eligible (PayPal falls back to visible if
+  eligibility cannot be determined); Pay Later gets its
+  `productCode`/`countryCode` and a `paypal-message` whose `amount` tracks
+  the bag total. All three share one session handler: `onApprove` only
+  shows confirmation on a 2xx capture, shows the decline message on 422,
+  and a pending notice on 202.
